+      - name: Decide what may still hold this pull request
+        id: verdict
+        continue-on-error: true
+        # `steps.ledger.outcome == 'success'` is load-bearing, not tidiness. A
+        # failed ledger read leaves /tmp/prev-ledger.md empty, which the rule
+        # reads as round 1 -- and round 1 judges only what THIS round's block
+        # says, so a finding carried on the ledger but not repeated in the block
+        # would stop being counted. Round 1 blocks more, not less, so the label
+        # would still be safe; the record behind it would not be. No ledger, no
+        # verdict.
